# Profile B: take BTF out of the image and ship it beside the image.
#
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF embeds the type information in the vmlinux, which is exactly what makes it
# always correct and always available. It also adds several megabytes, and a browser pays for
# those twice, once to download and once to decompress.
#
# So this profile builds without it and the BTF is generated separately from the vmlinux and
# served as its own file, which kxray fetches only when a lesson asks a question about types.
# The cost is that a lesson which needs types now needs a second download, and the boot is what
# gets faster.

# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF is not set
# CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF_MODULES is not set
